@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "use: [agents({ agents: ['orderAgent'], maxDelegations: 3, historyLength: 4 })],",
+  "cause": "The triage agent's agents() middleware lists only orderAgent, so the model is only given a delegate_to_orderAgent tool and has no way to reach refundAgent even though its system prompt says to delegate refunds to it.",
+  "evidence": "Before the fix, triage.chat().send('I want a refund for order A-1001, it arrived broken') returned \"I can't help you with refunds. Please contact customer support.\" The agents middleware creates one delegate_to_<name> tool per entry in its agents list (node_modules/@genkit-ai/middleware/lib/agents.js), so only delegate_to_orderAgent existed. After adding 'refundAgent' to the list, the same message produced a delegate_to_refundAgent call in the triage session, and refundAgent then ran lookupOrder and approveRefund (finishReason 'interrupted'), while order questions still delegate to orderAgent."
+}
